Content follows widely shared Vaishnava tradition: Ananta Shesha and the ocean of milk; Lakshmi; the common reading of
"Vishnu" as the all-pervading; shankha, chakra, gada, padma; Garuda; Vamana and Bali (Trivikrama, the three steps);
Sri Padmanabhaswamy Temple, Thiruvananthapuram, Kerala (the city's name taken as "city of Ananta"; the reclining deity
viewed through three doors); Bhagavad Gita 4.7-8 (paraphrased; "yada yada hi dharmasya" is the opening of 4.7);
the shaligram, fossil ammonites from the Kali Gandaki river, Nepal (Jurassic, roughly 150 million years old).
The temple, footprints and landscapes are painted from imagination, not drawn from the real sites.
Everything else (score, foley, paper, all painting) is original and generated in code for this film.
Rendering and tools: the Lemo-Opuscar style library (Watercolor Brush style) and its core/ tools.
